n USER_DB_PATH (/workspace/users.db) in the format: username:salt_hex:iterations:hash_hex\\n  - Provides functions: register_user(username, password) and authenticate_user(username, password)\\n  - Includes a small CLI for demonstration:\\n      - register <username> <password>\\n      - login <username> <password>\\n\\nHow to build and run (suggested steps):\\n1. Install OpenSSL development headers if not present (example for Debian/Ubuntu):\\n   - sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y libssl-dev build-essential\\n2. Compile:\\n   - gcc -o web_app /workspace/web_app.c -lcrypto\\n3. Register a user:\\n   - ./web_app register alice \"S3cureP@ssw0rd\"\\n   - This will append a line to /workspace/users.db\\n4. Authenticate:\\n   - ./web_app login alice \"S3cureP@ssw0rd\"\\n\\nSecurity & operational notes:\\n- After registering users, protect the DB: chmod 600 /workspace/users.db\\n- For concurrent access, add file locking (flock) when reading/writing the DB.\\n- Consider replacing the file DB with a real database and enable TLS in the web layer.\\n- Consider higher iteration counts or Argon2 for better resistance to GPU/ASIC attacks.\\n- Do not use this code in production without an independent security review.\\n\\nNext steps I can take (choose any):\\n- Compile the source and run a quick demo (I will ensure OpenSSL dev libs are installed before compiling).\\n- Add file locking and set safe file permissions automatically when creating the DB.\\n- Replace the file-based DB with SQLite and use prepared statements.\\n- Add unit tests for register/auth flows.\\n\\nI have completed the requested task of creating the C source file at /workspace/web_app.c. Would you like me to compile and run a short demo now?', action='finish')], inputs={}, outputs={}, agent_state=<AgentState.FINISHED: 'finished'>, resume_state=None, traffic_control_state=<TrafficControlState.NORMAL: 'normal'>, metrics=Metrics({'accumulated_cost': 0.01206215, 'costs': [{'model': 'gpt-5-mini', 'cost